e/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:21:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:33:10Z","body":"@kleonc I have uploaded my update with the newest commit. Since there is no image initialized (in _ready(), which is too early) when we call `get_image()`, we will need to synchronously generate the image. However, if we want to put the `write` (_set_texture_image()) under the `read-only` function `get_image()`, using `const_cast` is the only way that occurred to my mind. \r\n\r\nPlease let me know if you have a better way! Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797542552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797612345","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797612345","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797612345,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwC05","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:35:40Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:35:40Z","body":"> @kleonc I have uploaded my update with the newest commit. Since there is no image initialized when we call `get_image()`, we will need to synchronously generate the image. However, if we want to put the `write` (_set_texture_image()) under the `read-only` function `get_image()`, using `const_cast` is the only way shown in my mind.\r\n> \r\n> Please let me know if you have a better way! Thanks!\r\n\r\nYou can do what was done in #94744 (3e0d3c433bde1f2e0b18c3f05e43c3bf3c0804bc), which instead made the updating/generating fuctions be `const` (and thus callable without `const_cast` from within `get_image`).\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797612345/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797616826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797616826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797616826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwD66","user":{"login":"ytianle","id":61530469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTMwNDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61530469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle","html_url":"https://github.com/ytianle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:38:05Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:41:14Z","body":"> > @kleonc I have uploaded my update with the newest commit. Since there is no image initialized when we call `get_image()`, we will need to synchronously generate the image. However, if we want to put the `write` (_set_texture_image()) under the `read-only` function `get_image()`, using `const_cast` is the only way shown in my mind.\r\n> > Please let me know if you have a better way! Thanks!\r\n> \r\n> You can do what was done in #94744 ([3e0d3c4](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/3e0d3c433bde1f2e0b18c3f05e43c3bf3c0804bc)), which instead made the updating/generating functions be `const` (and thus callable without `const_cast` from within `get_image`).\r\n\r\nI have already tried this way, however, it is a method inherited from Texture2D. If we do not follow the signature, when the script is calling `get_image()`, our method with the new signature won't be triggered (it somehow calls the parent). I had already tested that. Please let me know if I understood sth wrong. Thanks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797616826/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797662622","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797662622","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797662622,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwPGe","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T17:59:40Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T17:59:40Z","body":"> I have already tried this way, however, it is a method inherited from Texture2D. If we do not follow the signature, when the script is calling `get_image()`, our method with the new signature won't be triggered (it somehow calls the parent). I had already tested that. Please let me know if I understood sth wrong. Thanks.\r\n\r\n`get_image` is inherited and its signature should be not changed indeed. :+1:\r\n\r\nWhat I meant is that changing e.g. these functions to `const` should be fine:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/modules/noise/noise_texture_2d.h#L70-L71\r\n\r\nJust like e.g. for GradientTexture1D these were changed to `const` (in #94744):\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/scene/resources/gradient_texture.h#L46\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/scene/resources/gradient_texture.h#L66\r\nand thus it can be called from `get_image` without `const_cast`:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/scene/resources/gradient_texture.cpp#L174-L180","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797662622/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797769923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797769923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797769923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwpTD","user":{"login":"ytianle","id":61530469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTMwNDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61530469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle","html_url":"https://github.com/ytianle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T18:47:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T18:47:59Z","body":"@kleonc If we follow the way you are mentioning, how can we solve the writing issue of the functions that use the `_set_texture_image` function? https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/scene/resources/gradient_texture.cpp#L61\r\nThis is the difference between `noise_texture_2d.cpp` and `gradient_texture.cpp`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797769923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797780600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797780600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797780600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mwr54","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T18:52:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T18:52:22Z","body":"It's true that this is different from GradientTexture. \r\nI left a comment in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105261#issuecomment-2797655130","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797780600/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797860475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797860475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797860475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mw_Z7","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T19:32:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T19:32:32Z","body":"> @kleonc If we follow the way you are mentioning, how can we solve the writing issue of the functions that use the `_set_texture_image` function?\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7b9c5122faafb6b4a655e31ae27bcffeb5cf254f/scene/resources/gradient_texture.cpp#L61\r\n> \r\n> This is the difference between `noise_texture_2d.cpp` and `gradient_texture.cpp`\r\n\r\nIndeed I wasn't aware about the differences between NoiseTexture2D and GradientTexture{1D|2D} when writing my previous comments (NoiseTexture2D emits `changed` signal when texture generation finishes, contrary to GradientTexture{1D|2D}). I'm not sure what's the exact solution we should go for.\r\n\r\nGiven https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105261#issuecomment-2797844123 / https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105261#issuecomment-2797838213 I'm not sure if the current behavior needs changing at all. I'd wait for more feedback from others.\r\n\r\n(@yuantianle Sorry for me not looking properly at the issue (#105261) before suggesting changes to the PR / proposed solution!)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797860475/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797875348","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105269#issuecomment-2797875348","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105269","id":2797875348,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mxDCU","user":{"login":"ytianle","id":61530469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNTMwNDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61530469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle","html_url":"https://github.com/ytianle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ytianle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T19:41:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T19:41:35Z","body":"No worries at all! Thanks for the suggestions, though!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797875348/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]